# Gemini CLI Grunt Worker

## Goal

Build a background system that executes "grunt work" tasks using Gemini CLI, freeing you to focus on critical thinking with Claude Opus 4.5.

---

## Architecture Overview

```
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                        TRIGGER SOURCES                         │
├────────────┬─────────────┬────────────────┬───────────────────┤
│ Telegram   │ Manual CLI  │ Nightly Agent  │ Sprint Queue      │
│ /grunt     │ grunt.py    │ (scheduled)    │ (auto-picked)     │
└─────┬──────┴──────┬──────┴───────┬────────┴─────────┬─────────┘
      │             │              │                  │
      ▼             ▼              ▼                  ▼
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                      TASK QUEUE                                │
│   .brain/ledger/grunt_queue.json                               │
│   [{ task, type, priority, context_files, status }]            │
└─────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────┘
                              │
                              ▼
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    GRUNT WORKER DAEMON                         │
│   scripts/grunt_worker.py                                      │
│                                                                │
│   1. Poll queue for pending tasks                              │
│   2. Classify task type → select context files                 │
│   3. Build Gemini CLI command with context                     │
│   4. Execute with premium model                                │
│   5. Save output to .brain/artifacts/grunt/                    │
│   6. Notify via Telegram                                       │
│   7. Check rate limits → pause if exceeded                     │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

