## Work Type Classification

### Types of Grunt Work

| Type | Description | Context Files Needed |
|:-----|:------------|:---------------------|
| `research` | Market research, competitor analysis | context.md |
| `summarize` | Summarize docs, PRs, articles | context.md + target doc |
| [test](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/scripts/nightly_agent.py#158-187) | Generate unit tests | context.md + target file + existing tests |
| `boilerplate` | CRUD endpoints, widgets, models | context.md + patterns + spec |
| `docs` | README, API docs, comments | context.md + target file |
| `refactor` | Code cleanup, formatting | target file + style guide |

### Classification Logic

```python
TASK_PATTERNS = {
    "research": ["research", "find", "analyze", "compare", "investigate"],
    "summarize": ["summarize", "tldr", "overview", "digest"],
    "test": ["test", "unittest", "spec", "coverage"],
    "boilerplate": ["create", "generate", "scaffold", "build", "widget", "endpoint"],
    "docs": ["document", "readme", "docstring", "api doc"],
    "refactor": ["refactor", "cleanup", "format", "lint"]
}

def classify_task(task_description: str) -> str:
    description_lower = task_description.lower()
    for task_type, keywords in TASK_PATTERNS.items():
        if any(kw in description_lower for kw in keywords):
            return task_type
    return "general"
```

